            <ArticleTitle>Early coronary artery stent restenosis: utility of percutaneous coronary angioscopy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>276-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Restenosis of an endovascular stent may be caused by thrombus, intimal hyperplasia, or extrinsic compression. Angiography may not adequately define the etiology of restenosis. We describe a patient in whom angioscopy proved important in diagnosing intimal hyperplasia obviating the need for thrombolytic therapy and prolonged anti-coagulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
